# Original request of the change
```
Issue #731: redactCredentialData leaves numeric values that are registered credentials

## Problem
`redactCredentialData` (src/util/proc.ts) redacts string values and keys that contain a registered credential, but leaves numbers alone. A credential made only of digits that a JSON number represents exactly is stored and published in full when it appears as a number. This was found in the review of #730 (worker agent-job events) and reproduced on main:

```ts
registerCredential("NUM_SECRET", "987654321012345");
redactCredentialData({ input: { token: 987654321012345, s: "987654321012345" } });
// → {"input":{"token":987654321012345,"s":"[redacted]"}}
```

The helper is shared, so every path that relies on it has the gap: agent events from the local harnesses (`tool_call.input`), stored events, MCP results and worker events.

## Requirements
- In `redactCredentialData`, a number whose canonical string form (`String(n)`) contains a registered credential, or is contained in one (the same rule that applies to strings), becomes the string `"[redacted]"`. Other numbers are unchanged.
- Tests:
  - an all-digit credential as a number, nested in an object and in an array, is redacted;
  - unrelated numbers are unchanged;
  - an all-digit credential that is too large to be an exact JSON number still redacts as a string.

## Out of scope
Other encodings (#335), credential registration rules.

Budget: about 10 lines plus tests.

Closes #731
```

